<blockquote class="inline_help">
Service auto-starts with array. Changes apply after clicking Apply and will restart the service if it is running.

<strong>Dynamic collection</strong> lets the agent decide when each collector runs: on change events where the source
has them, faster while a client is consuming the data, and slowly otherwise. Turn it off to set the intervals below
yourself; your saved intervals are kept in both modes. <code>GET /api/v1/collectors/status</code> shows what each
collector does right now.

Hardware-dependent collectors (GPU, Network Cards &amp; Optics, UPS, NUT, ZFS, Storage Topology) follow hardware
detection: the agent checks for the hardware at startup, every 15 minutes and on <strong>Re-check hardware</strong>.
While the hardware is absent the collector is off and its row is hidden, whatever its setting; the setting is kept and
applies again once the hardware is detected. With the hardware present, <strong>Auto</strong> runs the collector every
5 minutes, an explicit interval runs it at that interval, and <strong>Disabled</strong> keeps it off.
<strong>Show all collectors</strong> only reveals hidden rows — it never turns a collector on. If hardware detection is
unavailable (for example the agent is stopped), every row is shown.
</blockquote>

